# Atlas Program KB {#atlas}

## Goals {.section} ^sec-goals

### EU Launch {.goal #eu-launch} ^g1
target:: 2026-09-15

## Decisions {.section} ^sec-dec

### Choose Stripe as payment provider {.decision #choose-stripe} ^d1
status:: accepted
date:: 2026-05-10
cites:: [[PCI Compliance Audit 2026]]

Lower fees and stronger EU coverage than the incumbent.

### Use event sourcing for the billing ledger {.decision #event-sourcing} ^d2
status:: accepted
date:: 2026-05-22
cites:: [[Latency Report Q2]]

Append-only ledger simplifies audit and replay.

### Deprecate the legacy REST API {.decision #deprecate-rest} ^d3
status:: proposed
date:: 2026-06-03
cites:: [[User Research June]]

Interviewees rely on the new endpoints already.

### Ship the EU region first {.decision #eu-first} ^d4
status:: accepted
date:: 2026-06-11
cites:: [[User Research June]]

Largest waitlisted cohort is in the EU.

### Adopt Postgres 16 for the ledger store {.decision #postgres-16} ^d5
status:: superseded
date:: 2026-04-18
cites:: [[Latency Report Q2]]

Superseded by the event sourcing decision.

## Open Questions {.section} ^sec-q

### Do we need SOC2 certification before launch? {.question #soc2} ^q1
status:: open

Until answered this [blocks:: [[Run the penetration test]]].

### Can the exporter reuse the ledger schema? {.question #exporter-schema} ^q2
status:: open

Until answered this [blocks:: [[Build the invoice PDF exporter]]].

### Is the latency budget 200ms or 300ms? {.question #latency-budget} ^q3
status:: resolved

### Who signs the Stripe contract? {.question #stripe-contract} ^q4
status:: open

Until answered this [blocks:: [[Integrate the Stripe checkout flow]]].

## Workstream: Billing {.section} ^ws1

### Integrate the Stripe checkout flow {.task #stripe-checkout} ^t1
status:: doing
priority:: high
due:: 2026-08-05
owned-by:: [[Alice Chen]]

Covers hosted checkout and webhook handling. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Choose Stripe as payment provider]]].

### Migrate historical invoices to the ledger {.task #migrate-invoices} ^t2
status:: todo
priority:: high
due:: 2026-08-20
owned-by:: [[Alice Chen]]

Backfill of roughly forty thousand historical invoices. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Integrate the Stripe checkout flow]]] and [depends-on:: [[Use event sourcing for the billing ledger]]].

### Notify customers about the billing change {.task #notify-customers} ^t3
status:: todo
priority:: med
due:: 2026-09-01
owned-by:: [[Dev Patel]]

Email plus in-app banner announcement. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Migrate historical invoices to the ledger]]].

### Reconcile refunds against the old system {.task #reconcile-refunds} ^t4
status:: todo
priority:: low
owned-by:: [[Dev Patel]]

Reconciliation window is the last two fiscal years. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Migrate historical invoices to the ledger]]].

### Build the invoice PDF exporter {.task #invoice-exporter} ^t5
status:: todo
priority:: med
owned-by:: [[Alice Chen]]

Exports must match the ledger totals exactly.

### Set up billing alerts and dashboards {.task #billing-alerts} ^t6
status:: done
priority:: low
owned-by:: [[Dev Patel]]

Dashboards live in the shared observability space.

### Localize the checkout UI for German {.task #localize-german} ^t18
status:: todo
priority:: med
owned-by:: [[Alice Chen]]
part-of:: [[EU Launch]]

Covers currency, date formats, and checkout copy. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Integrate the Stripe checkout flow]]].

## Workstream: Search {.section} ^ws2

### Rebuild the search indexing pipeline {.task #search-indexing} ^t7
status:: doing
priority:: high
due:: 2026-08-12
owned-by:: [[Bob Marsh]]

Replaces the nightly batch indexer with streaming updates.

### Add typo tolerance to product search {.task #typo-tolerance} ^t8
status:: todo
priority:: med
owned-by:: [[Bob Marsh]]

Uses edit-distance matching for product names. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Rebuild the search indexing pipeline]]].

### Benchmark query latency at ten times load {.task #latency-benchmark} ^t9
status:: done
priority:: high
owned-by:: [[Bob Marsh]]

Load profile mirrors the June traffic snapshot.

### Ship the search relevance A/B test {.task #relevance-ab} ^t10
status:: todo
priority:: med
owned-by:: [[Dev Patel]]

Experiment runs on ten percent of traffic. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Add typo tolerance to product search]]].

### Archive the old search cluster {.task #archive-cluster} ^t11
status:: todo
priority:: low
owned-by:: [[Bob Marsh]]

Cluster is kept read-only for thirty days first. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Rebuild the search indexing pipeline]]].

### Cache hot queries at the edge {.task #edge-cache} ^t12
status:: doing
priority:: med
owned-by:: [[Carol Diaz]]

Cache keys include region and locale. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Ship the EU region first]]].

## Workstream: Platform {.section} ^ws3

### Provision the EU data region {.task #eu-region} ^t13
status:: doing
priority:: high
due:: 2026-08-01
owned-by:: [[Carol Diaz]]
part-of:: [[EU Launch]]

Region is provisioned in Frankfurt. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Ship the EU region first]]].

### Set up GDPR data-retention jobs {.task #gdpr-retention} ^t14
status:: todo
priority:: high
due:: 2026-08-25
owned-by:: [[Erin Fox]]
part-of:: [[EU Launch]]

Retention defaults to ninety days for event data. Gated by [depends-on:: [[Provision the EU data region]]].

### Run the penetration test {.task #pentest} ^t15
status:: todo
priority:: high
owned-by:: [[Erin Fox]]
part-of:: [[EU Launch]]

Scope covers the public API and the admin console.

### Automate blue-green deploys {.task #blue-green} ^t16
status:: done
priority:: med
owned-by:: [[Carol Diaz]]

Cutover rehearsed in the staging environment.

### Rotate all production secrets {.task #rotate-secrets} ^t17
status:: done
priority:: high
owned-by:: [[Erin Fox]]

Rotation includes database and third-party credentials.

